---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Code of Conduct | Rust India"
  description="All Rust India spaces are welcoming, inclusive, and harassment-free. Report issues to team@rustindia.org."
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath="/conduct/" />

  <main class="site-main">
    <article class="section-shell conduct">
      <header class="page-header">
        <p class="section-label">Community</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Code of Conduct</h1>
        <p class="page-lede">Every Rust India space — chat channels, events, meetups, and the blog — is a welcoming, harassment-free space.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Our expectations</h2>
        <p>We expect everyone in Rust India spaces to be:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Respectful</strong> — treat people with courtesy, even when you disagree. Disagreement is fine; personal attacks are not.</li>
          <li><strong>Inclusive</strong> — welcome people of all backgrounds, experience levels, and identities. Beginners are the future of this community.</li>
          <li><strong>Constructive</strong> — share feedback and criticism in good faith, focused on ideas rather than people.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Unacceptable behaviour</h2>
        <p>Harassment, discrimination, intimidation, and any form of abusive behaviour are not tolerated in any Rust India space, online or in person. This includes unwelcome sexual attention, offensive language, and public or private harassment.</p>

        <h2>Reporting</h2>
        <p>If you experience or witness a violation, contact the community team at <a href="mailto:team@rustindia.org">team@rustindia.org</a>. Reports are handled confidentially and seriously. If the incident involves an event or meetup, you may also approach any organiser on site.</p>

        <h2>The official Rust code of conduct</h2>
        <p>Rust India follows the spirit of the official <a href="https://www.rust-lang.org/policies/code-of-conduct" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Rust Code of Conduct</a>. Where this page and the official document differ, the more protective standard applies.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .conduct {
    max-width: min(46rem, var(--shell-width));
  }

  .prose {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin: 0.35rem 0;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
